[16] STORAGE
     type: high-capacity disk array / SAN-style storage
     role: stores large data volumes for the servers

[09] LOAD BALANCER
     type: traffic distribution appliance
     role: spreads incoming requests across multiple servers

[06] UPS
     type: Uninterruptible Power Supply
     role: provides backup power during outages

[01] PDU
     type: Power Distribution Unit
     role: distributes conditioned power to every device in the rack

FUNDAMENTALS
- Rack units (U): height is measured in 1.75-inch increments (1U, 2U, etc.)
- Front-to-back airflow: cool intake at front, hot exhaust at rear
- Cable management: patch panel + structured cabling keeps the rack serviceable
- Power path: PDU feeds devices; UPS sits upstream for failover
- Security path: firewall sits between switch/WAN and the servers
- Compute vs storage: servers process; NAS/storage persist data
- High availability: load balancer + multiple identical servers reduce single points of failure
